  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/parotocinclus_jumbo_lda_25_pitbull_pleco_en/",
      "html": "<p>Parotocinclus jumbo is one of the largest species of the genus (maximum size is reported to be around 6-7 cm) and one of the prettiest. It is an algae eater.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/parotocinclus_jumbo_lda_25_pitbull_pleco_en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/parotocinclus_jumbo_lda_25_pitbull_pleco_en/",
      "html": "<p>There is very obvious sexual dichromatism in this species, which has so far not been reported in the aquarium literature. Males get wonderful shining, blueish-green saddles on the back which are missing in females. In addition, the females are much more plump than the males.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/parotocinclus_jumbo_lda_25_pitbull_pleco_en/",
      "html": "<p>There are some spawning reports on the species. It seems to have a positive effect if a rainy season is simulated, as is done with many Corydoras species. In practice this means large water changes with cooler and softer water than the water used for regular keeping. However, the temperature difference should not be too big; about 5°C is suitable.</p><p>The fish does not practise brood care in any way. The eggs are sticky and become attached to the glass or tank equipment – again there are many parallels to Corydoras. It is reported that raising the spawn is rather difficult and that the eggs tend to get fungus.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/parotocinclus_jumbo_lda_25_pitbull_pleco_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Parotocinclus: ancient Greek, means \"alike Otocinclus\"; Otocinclus is another genus of catfish. jumbo: refers to the unusual size of the species compared with other members of the genus.</p>"
    }
  ],
